    {
      "id": "kukg3xf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Exam Notes"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Article 32 is the very heart and soul of the Indian Constitution, without which this Constitution would be a nullity.",
      "id": "0mkl3lw"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 14 ensures Equality Before Law and Equal Protection of the Laws within the territory of India.",
        "Article 21 guarantees Protection of Life and Personal Liberty, expanded by the Judiciary to include the Right to Privacy and Education.",
        "Article 32 gives citizens the Right to Constitutional Remedies through five types of writs: Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari, and Quo-Warranto.",
        "Article 108 provides for a Joint Sitting of both Houses of Parliament summoned by the President in case of deadlock on a bill.",
        "Article 368 confers the power upon Parliament to amend the Constitution and prescribes the procedure for it."
      ],
      "id": "8hw06il"
    },
